{"content":[{"c":["BEZEK"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Site of a major victory for the tribes of Simeon and Judah over the Perizzites and Canaanites (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.3-7","r":"Judg.1.3-7","rawR":"Judg.1.3-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.3-7","value":"Judg.1.3-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:3-7"},"). Adoni-bezek, which means “lord of Bezek,” was king of the city at that time. Bezek was perhaps located at Khirbet Bezqa, a few miles northwest of Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Place where Saul gathered an army to attack the Ammonites who were troubling Jabesh-gilead (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.11.8-11","r":"1Sam.11.8-11","rawR":"1Sam.11.8-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.11.8-11","value":"1Sam.11.8-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 11:8-11"},"). This Bezek is usually located at Khirbet Ibziq, a little south of Mt Gilboa."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bezek","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:3-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.3-7","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.3-7","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.3-7"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 11:8-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.11.8-11","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.11.8-11","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.11.8-11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"254fd35f3335f32807d33aa0d7ef3cfbc0fffd1e9b4a870b12b7e31a0175b14c","sourceItemName":"Bezek","sourceItemOrder":295,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bezek","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bezek","title":"Bezek","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}